    {
      "text": "shall a man leave his father and his mother, Gen. 2:24 (Mark 10:7; Moses 3:24; Abr. 5:18). took of the fruit … and gave also unto her husband, Gen. 3:6. thy desire shall be to thy husband, Gen. 3:16 (Moses 4:22). Isaac entreated the Lord for his wife, Gen. 25:21. a bloody husband art thou, Ex. 4:25. thou shalt not covet thy neighbour’s wife, Ex. 20:17 (D&C 19:25). man hath taken a new wife … shall cheer up his wife, Deut. 24:5. husband’s brother … perform the duty of an husband’s brother, Deut. 25:5. rejoice with the wife of thy youth, Prov. 5:18. virtuous woman is a crown to her husband, Prov. 12:4. heart of her husband doth safely trust in her, Prov. 31:11. Live joyfully with the wife whom thou lovest, Eccl. 9:9. thy Maker is thine husband, Isa. 54:5. taketh strangers instead of her husband, Ezek. 16:32. let none deal treacherously against the wife of his youth, Mal. 2:15.",
